    {
      "id": "rn_34xmznRtwfxFVBrv::L2::Q8",
      "moduleId": "rn_34xmznRtwfxFVBrv::L2",
      "stem": "Explain why a nerve cell's axon needs its fatty sheath AND its length to do one job.",
      "misconceptionClass": "axon design reasoning",
      "kind": "explain-why",
      "modelAnswer": "Length carries the impulse between distant regions, while the fatty sheath insulates the axon so the signal travels fast and does not leak away; together they turn a cell into a working cable between body parts and the central nervous system.",
